%N A107290 a(n) = (M_n + 2)/3 where M_n is the n-th Mersenne prime.
%C A107290 Many small values are primes; (M_89+2)/3 is the first composite.
%H A107290 Amiram Eldar, <a href="/A107290/b107290.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 2..18</a>
%H A107290 Chris K. Caldwell, <a href="https://t5k.org/glossary/page.php?sort=NewMersenneConjecture">New Mersenne Prime Conjecture</a>, The Prime Glossary.
%F A107290 a(n) = (A000668(n) + 2)/3.
%t A107290 a[n_] := (2^MersennePrimeExponent[n] + 1)/3; Array[a, 11, 2] (* _Amiram Eldar_, Oct 03 2026 *)
